    "description": "Designer/developer with key role in several of Cadence's strongest products, including C to Silicon, OpenAccess, Virtuoso, and Relative Object Design.\n\n2007-2008 Software Architect for C to Silicon product.\n\n2000-2007 Software Engineer / Architect for the OpenAccess database. \n\nProject leader for hierarchical technology database project. This involves creating a single technology database view from multiple, distributed databases. The team included eight engineers plus support personnel. Responsible for the functional spec, the implementation spec, a significant portion of the implementation, and oversight of the rest of the implementation, testing, and delivery of the new features. \n\nResponsible for the design and implementation of the data management sub-system for the OpenAccess database. This included the plug-in interface which allows users to develop their own data management plug-in modules. This project also included the design and development of the internal data management plug-in, which uses a client/server approach to controlling multi-user library access. The client/server communication is implemented using TCP/IP sockets.\n\nResponsible for the design and implementation of the undo sub-system for the OpenAccess database.\n\n1995-2000 R&D Manager / Senior Software Engineer, Virtuoso Product Line\n\nAs R&D manager, directly managed engineering personnel, defined product direction, interfaced with architects, support teams and external product groups, led the cross-functional team and interacted with customers.\n\nAs software engineer, originated and developed concept for Relative Object Design. This is a high level extension language which significantly reduces the development complexity for engineers who use programmable cells for layout. Participated in the design, implementation and release of this project,. This project received many customer accolades for enabling productivity improvements in programmable cell development.",
